    <string name="about_text">Every platform runs the same C++ core: identical deterministic formulas (no platform math library), the same GLSL ES 3.00 shaders, a fixed 1920×1080 offscreen resolution and a fixed 1/60 s timestep per frame. Worker threads simulate frame N+1 and write directly into mapped GPU buffers while the GPU renders frame N; fences guard a triple-buffered ring so neither side stalls. Verification hashes prove that the calculations are bit-identical across devices.</string>
